  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-89068",
      "knowledge_point_id": "e6e4940d-fc80-563d-85a2-b83478cce6c5",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Vertical Hyperbola Given Algebraically",
      "problem": "What are the parametric equations of the hyperbola $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}=1?$",
      "worked_solution": "The parametric equations of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=\\sqrt{25}=5$ and $b=\\sqrt{16}=4.$ Therefore, the parametric equations are\n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=5\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$",
