  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-106617",
      "knowledge_point_id": "e538c21e-67fd-56f7-b09f-a9fec3121f78",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Vertical Hyperbola Given Graphically",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062908/assets/6044a47f621612d56138893be089f48a2d2a7060c13d044086154ab7892fac38.png)\n\nFind the parametric equations of the hyperbola shown above given that its asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{1}{2}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "The parametric equations of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by \n\n$$\nx=b\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=a\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are positive constants.\n\nThe vertices of the hyperbola occur at $(0,\\pm a).$ From the graph, we have that $(0,1)$ is a vertex of the hyperbola, so $a=1.$\n\nRecall also that the asymptotes of the hyperbola occur at $y=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.$ In our case, the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{1}{2}x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{a}{b} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{b} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ b & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t.\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,y=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,\\,y=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
