  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-127526",
      "knowledge_point_id": "1e118393-2388-5add-b516-e565abe1e36a",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to an Ellipse",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062909/assets/e4c39b409f6049a4fdead506c329d232820876c37ede9540adfeade2d7c1b9dc.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above.",
      "worked_solution": "Since our ellipse is centered at $(3,0)$ and has semiaxes $3$ and $2,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-0)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2(x-3)}{9}+\\frac{2y}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{y}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2(x-3)}{9} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{4(x-3)}{9y}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{9x}{4(y-3)}",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-\\frac{4(x-3)}{9y}",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{2(x-3)}{3y}",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-\\frac{3y}{2(x-3)}",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
