  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-73015",
      "knowledge_point_id": "231604dc-fe8f-59be-90fe-37af7a1bb648",
      "knowledge_point": "Identifying When a Rational Function has no Vertical Asymptotes",
      "problem": "Find the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}{2x+4}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's simplify the expression by factoring both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}{2x+4} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}(x+2)}{2(x+2)}=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the denominator is never zero, we conclude that this function has no vertical asymptotes. A plot of the function is below. Note that it is not defined at $x=-2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/assets/3ad83a79ccd47d9d035ac5a3f47b929a1e6b3939cdaddee9ff0f2d6a3cf07e56.png)",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x=2",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x=-10",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "No vertical asymptotes",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x=-2",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$x=0$, $x=-2$",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "knowledge_point_source_id": 86,
      "difficulty": "moderate",
      "provenance": {
        "activity_question": "question-73015",
        "kp_title": "Identifying When a Rational Function has no Vertical Asymptotes",
        "kp_href": "/topics/1815#86"
      },
      "topic_id": 1815,
      "source_file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/state.json",
