  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063579",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-160037",
      "knowledge_point_id": "1bbe2fe7-b69c-54f3-9f1c-3369e3f1395d",
      "knowledge_point": "Solving for Unknowns By Computing a Product and Equating Real and Imaginary Parts",
      "problem": "Given that $3+5\\text{i}=\\frac{p+\\text{i}q}{1-\\text{i}},$ calculate $p$ and $q.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we multiply both sides of the equation by $1-\\text{i}$ to get rid of the fraction and isolate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3+5\\text{i} & =\\frac{p+\\text{i}q}{1-\\text{i}} \\\\ (3+5\\text{i})(1-\\text{i}) & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ 3-3\\text{i}+5\\text{i}-5{\\text{i}}^{2} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ 3+5+2\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q \\\\ 8+2\\text{i} & =p+\\text{i}q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get\n\n$$\n8=p.\n$$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =q.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=8$ and $q=2.$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$p=-4$, $q=2$",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$p=-3$, $q=2$",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$p=2$, $q=1$",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$p=8$, $q=2$",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$p=2$, $q=3$",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "knowledge_point_source_id": 5261,
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "provenance": {
        "activity_question": "question-160037",
        "kp_title": "Solving for Unknowns By Computing a Product and Equating Real and Imaginary Parts",
        "kp_href": "/topics/159#5261"
      },
